INT. ORBITAL GREENHOUSE - ARTIFICIAL DAY

A long curved hall of racks and tubes. Green leaves in violet grow-light. Condensation beads on every pipe. Earth hangs in the viewport, small and blue.

ANJALI VERMA, 50s, the commander, silver-haired, stands at the central console. Her coveralls are stained with soil.

KOFI BAAH, 30s, botanist, kneels at a rack of wilted tomato vines. He holds a leaf up to the light.

LENKA HORVAT, 40s, engineer, hangs upside-down from a ceiling rail. A toolkit floats beside her.

SOLOMON ECK, 60s, the crew's cook, sits alone in the corner with a mug of tea, watching them.

The ventilation fans RATTLE and slow. Then they stop.

ANJALI
Status.

LENKA
Fans three through seven are dead.

KOFI
That's the whole east wing.

ANJALI
Can you fix it?

LENKA
Maybe. I need twenty minutes.

SOLOMON
(to no one)
We don't have twenty minutes.

ANJALI
Solomon?

SOLOMON
Oxygen scrubbers. Ask me how I know.

She does not. She taps the console. Red text flickers.

ANJALI
Everyone, listen. We're going to move the plants to the west wing. One rack at a time. Kofi, you're lead.

KOFI
Understood.

He rises. He pulls a rack toward the hatch. It sticks. He braces his boot and heaves. It slides.

Lenka drops from the rail, grabs the opposite side. Together they push.

Solomon puts down his mug. He joins them without a word.

Anjali watches them move. She exhales.

ANJALI (CONT'D)
(to herself)
Thank God for stubborn people.

LENKA
What was that?

ANJALI
Nothing.

The fans cough back to life. A low whir. Fresh air stirs the leaves.

KOFI
Lenka?

LENKA
I didn't touch anything.

SOLOMON
Maybe it likes us.

ANJALI
It's a greenhouse, Solomon.

SOLOMON
So it's alive.

She smiles. She shakes her head. The viewport blue glows over all four.
